hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1699","\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, who said: al-Mustamir ibn al-Rayyan al-Ayadi informed us, who said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the world and said:\n\n*\Indeed"","" the world is green and sweet. Beware of it and beware of women.\""*\n\nThen he (ﷺ) mentioned three women from the Children of Israel: two tall women who were well-known"","" and a short woman who was not well-known. She fashioned two wooden legs for herself and made a ring"","" filling it with the finest musk perfume"","" and placed a cover over it. Whenever she passed by the mosque or a gathering"","" she would open it"","" and its fragrance would spread.\n\nAl-Mustamir (RA) moved his left pinky finger slightly forward"","" leaving three fingers folded"","" and said: *\""This is how she was lifted up"","" leaving those three (fingers folded).\""*"""""
"1700","Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Ala’:\nSufyan narrated to us;\nal-A‘mash narrated to us, from ‘Umarah — and he is Ibn ‘Umayr —, from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that ‘Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud (RA) would say when he saw women:\n\Keep them back where Allah has placed them.\""\nHe also said:\n\""Indeed"","" they were with the Children of Israel"","" lining up with the men. A woman would wear a high shoe so that her ankle would be exposed to her beloved. So they were afflicted with menstruation"","" and mosques were forbidden to them.\""\n\nAnd when ‘Abd Allah (RA) would see them"","" he would say:\n\""Keep them back where Allah has placed them.\""\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) said:\n\""The report is *mawquf* (stopped at the Companion) and not *musnad* (connected to the Prophet ﷺ).\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
